    <!-- Guide dialog -->
    <string name="guide_title">HoloCube Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_text">Start Inference: run transmitter recognition on live camera frames. At most one box labelled Transmitter with its confidence percentage is drawn: the strongest valid detection above the threshold.\n\nRecord: save a training video (MP4 with microphone audio) to Movies/HoloCube. Tap Stop to finish.\n\nTransmitter: show the HoloCube optical pattern full screen in landscape at maximum brightness, keeping the display awake. Tap the pattern for About Us; swipe from a screen edge to return.\n\n+ / −: zoom. ↺: switch camera. C: clear results and restart the camera.\n\nSettings: confidence threshold and PyTorch CPU threads. Settings → In-Device Local File Inference opens a test image stored on this phone (for example in Pictures/HoloCube Test Dataset) and runs the Transmitter Detection Model on it, showing the box, its confidence, and the inference time. Sharing an image to HoloCube opens the same screen.\n\nThe trained holocube_transmitter.pt checkpoint runs on this phone with embedded Python and PyTorch. No server or model download is needed.</string>
    <string name="ok">OK</string>

